reads.setup:
Notation: (k⊗L) is a k-layer transformer block looped L times. The whole block (attention plus FFN) is tied. There is no input injection, no per-loop embedding and no change of loop count at test time: every model is evaluated at the L it was trained with. Each looped model is compared with an iso-param baseline (k⊗1) and an iso-FLOP baseline (kL⊗1), which has the same depth and L times the parameters.

Synthetic tasks (Section 2, A.1):
(a) Addition of n 3-digit numbers, trained on a mixture n∈{2,4,8,16,32}. d=256, 8 heads, FFN 1024, Adafactor, batch 1024, lr 0.005, 200k steps. Each cell is the best of 3 seeds.
(b) p-hop induction: alphabet 4, length 256, p=16/32, 4M training examples, d=128, FFN 512.
(c) i-GSM: symbolic DAG of depth 4, arithmetic mod 7, 4M training examples, 50k test, d=128.

Language modelling (Section 3, A.2): the Pile, batch 512 × 1280 tokens, 400k steps with a cosine schedule, peak LR 0.01 tuned on the baseline and reused unchanged for looped and shallow models. The baseline is a 24-layer decoder with d=2048, FFN 5120 and 32 heads; the text says 1B, A.2 says 1.5B. Looped and shallow variants change only the layer count; k∈{4,6,8,12} looped 24/k times, plus a 'middle loop' (4⊗1,4,1). Evaluations, all single seed:
- validation perplexity;
- closed-book QA (TriviaQA, TydiQA-NoContext, NQ, WebQuestions), which the authors call 'memorization';
- open-book QA (TydiQA-GoldP, SQuADv2, DROP, QuAC, CoQA);
- 6 math word problem tasks, 5-shot;
- 4 'reasoning primitives' (depth-0 and depth-1 variable assignment, math and code variants), 5-shot.

Analysis tools:
- %Gap = (looped − iso-param)/(iso-FLOP − iso-param).
- Isoplots: downstream score against log-perplexity at checkpoints every 20k steps from step 120k, with a linear fit.
- Depth scaling: (4⊗L) for L∈{1,2,3,6,9,12} against (4L⊗1), fitting Acc = α log D + β and reporting α_loop/α_base.

Section 4 regularizer: a cosine-similarity penalty between corresponding parameter groups of successive k-layer blocks of the 24-layer model, λ∈{1,10}, k∈{4,6,8,12}.

Theory (Section 5, App B), all expressivity constructions with hand-set finite-precision weights:
- a 1-layer block looped ⌈log2 n⌉ times composes n group elements;
- a looped 1-layer block simulates any L-layer model with R distinct layers;
- p-hop is solvable with ⌊log2 p⌋+2 loops;
- m loops simulate m chain-of-thought (CoT) steps.

FFNs are ReLU in the theory. The LM FFN type is not stated. There is no FFN-only looping and no comparison of FFN types.
